From fb14f9b6937cb2390d954cfac5f51156a2e2994d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 20:32:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix aggregate store-forwarding: never forward a register
 parameter's home slot

forward_store_only_temporaries treats 'memcpy dest, root' where root is a
store-only entry alloca as a redirectable snapshot. But the entry-block
allocas that home register parameters are written by the PROLOGUE, not by
IR-visible stores (find_param_alloca maps param i to the i-th entry-block
alloca; the x86 prologue spills %xmm0.. there directly). For
'void dump(const char*, __m128 v)' the v-home alloca has ZERO IR stores, so
the pass found nothing to redirect, deleted the 'memcpy tmp, v_home'
snapshot as 'forwarded', and tmp stayed uninitialized: every out-of-line
call printed stack garbage.

REPRODUCER (tests/intrinsics t128_fp/t512_int, present on upstream main):
4+ distinct _mm_*_ps calls through one dump helper; the first three call
sites are inlined (bug masked), the 4th+ goes out-of-line and prints
garbage lanes ('div: 8.07e-43 ...' instead of '0.5 1 1.5 2').
CCC_NO_AGG_COPY_FWD=1 healed it; new sub-pass gates (CCC_NO_AGG_STORE_FWD /
CCC_NO_AGG_MAIN / CCC_NO_AGG_DEAD_STORES) isolated the store-only
forwarding; CCC_AGG_FWD_SKIP_FN narrowed it to dump128.

FIX: exclude the first params.len() entry-block allocas (the parameter
home slots, exactly the find_param_alloca convention) as forwarding
sources. Fail closed: this only suppresses an optimization on slots with
implicit prologue writes.

PROOF: intrinsics differential suite 1/3 -> 3/3 vs GCC; new regression
test agg_fwd_param_home.c (self-checking, needs 4 call sites); full
battery green: 653 lib, 162 regression, 50 correctness, 86 linker.
